{"id": "EUVD-2026-86677", "enisaUuid": "70d2032b-19ec-310f-a79e-c8c47499529b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ns390/ism: folio_put() after error\n\ndmb->cpu_addr was allocated via folio_alloc(). Use folio_put() instead of\nkfree() in the error exit of ism_alloc_dmb() to avoid slab allocator\ncorruption.\n\nWhile at it, reset dmb->cpu_addr after folio_put to avoid unintentional UAF\nby future callers.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:23:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:12:29", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/90f6f5cb331af52b14c0f309fb27dc243e8e2982", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/890e2ef726904d1d8328e4b9f5090eeb8761b9d1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/eebb6a9017b55ac05be770cf7b89f9da49505ae7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/60983356fab0c1171c5cb1b56a36349ebadc608e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/907a56ab3eb8a58500a58daa76087f17bb2b6826"], "aliases": ["GHSA-8x93-8jfm-fwvw", "CVE-2026-98024"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0ad8d8c0-78ec-3b89-b74d-9d66fe461f65", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "14047c0d-cbab-3f46-be45-30a229dadf8e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "2ed1f850-5876-36fa-b1e9-70497363acbc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.9"}, {"id": "2f96e3ed-a634-3b18-a5f5-2fe9bbcf0740", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.29 <6.6.158"}, {"id": "44df801a-6d86-3dab-9151-6bff9b1cd629", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "83781384a96b95e2b6403d3c8a002b2c89031770 <907a56ab3eb8a58500a58daa76087f17bb2b6826"}, {"id": "5d5e74b5-309d-33c5-bca5-660d38535aef", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "6601fcbf-0